# Backend URL (Server-side). The Go backend (`backend/`) is the sole thing that talks to GraphDB
# directly now — SPARQL_ENDPOINT_URL/SPARQL_USER/SPARQL_PASSWORD moved to backend/.env.example's
# GRAPHDB_ENDPOINT_URL/GRAPHDB_USER/GRAPHDB_PASSWORD. See backend/README.md to run it.
BACKEND_URL=http://localhost:8090

# Signed JWT this app sends as `Authorization: Bearer <token>` on every request it forwards to the
# backend (spec/threat-mitigation/plan.md, Story 004) — the backend rejects unauthenticated calls
# with 401. Mint one with `importctl mint-token --sub frontend-app` (backend/README.md). Deliberately
# NOT `PUBLIC_`-prefixed — it must never reach the browser bundle.
BACKEND_AUTH_TOKEN=

# User identity for the Query Workbench (query-workbench STORY-179): a JWT standing in for the token an
# IdP would issue after login elsewhere. The SvelteKit server DECODES it (no signature check — it has
# no signing secret) to read `sub` and an optional `name` claim; only those two reach the browser. It
# is never sent to the backend — BACKEND_AUTH_TOKEN above stays the service credential. Mint one with
# `importctl mint-token --sub alice`. Optional: when empty, browsing/querying still work but saving
# queries and annotating are disabled. Deliberately NOT `PUBLIC_`-prefixed.
USER_AUTH_TOKEN=

# Default namespace configuration (client-visible — read via $env/dynamic/public, so this must be
# prefixed with PUBLIC_). Leave unset to use this app's built-in default (see src/lib/config.ts).
# Every other namespace value (the default namespace's base IRI, its three storage graphs, and its
# IRI-minting prefix) is derived from this single value (STORY-025) — it replaces the old
# independently-configured PUBLIC_SHAPES_NAMESPACE/PUBLIC_SCHEMA_GRAPH vars. Quote the value if it
# ends in "#" — dotenv otherwise reads an unquoted trailing "#" as a comment marker and silently
# truncates it.
PUBLIC_SCHEMA_NAMESPACE="http://ld.pageagent.com/rdf-schema-editor/schema#"
